  "term": "cosmetic surgery",
  "definition": "Cosmetic surgery refers to surgical procedures sought to change appearance and sometimes to repair deformities that cause functional problems. In the psychology context, it is discussed as a choice that may be linked to self-esteem, body dissatisfaction, and social influences, while also carrying risks and possible complications.",
